 # Light Ray Sampling
 
-Also called: Light Ray Marching
+Also called: Light Ray Marching, Ray Marching with Light Sampling
 
 ## Overview
-Light Ray Sampling computes the direct illumination at a surface or volume sample point by stepping along the direction to a light source (typically a distant sun) to the light's boundary, accumulating optical density, and applying the phase function [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard shadow ray tracing by explicitly integrating the participating medium's extinction and scattering properties along the light path, rather than performing a single binary occlusion test [S1, S3, unofficial].
+Light Ray Sampling computes direct illumination at a sample point by stepping along the direction to a light source (typically a distant sun) to the light's boundary, accumulating optical density, and applying the phase function [S2, unofficial]. It differs from standard shadow ray tracing by explicitly integrating the participating medium's extinction and scattering properties along the light path, rather than performing a single binary occlusion test [S2, unofficial].
 
